    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d954">

                <pb facs="0736" n="620" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg620"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13770.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Silliman to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-13T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 13, 1914, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Generally speaking the Carranza generals appear to have allied themselves with
                    him yesterday as against the Convention on the presumption that Villa will not
                    be eliminated. Convention appears to have committed itself to Villa, appointing
                    him Commander-in-Chief, and has declared Carranza in rebellion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
